WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.370
Narrator: In one hospital in Barcelona,

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.500
patients recovering from COVID-19

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.423
are relearning basic motor skills.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:09.150
There's still so much we don't know

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.360
about the novel coronavirus.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.510
Experts are confident that it
primarily attacks the lungs,

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.990
but more and more scientists

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.010
are finding other lingering effects,

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:20.720
even in the brain.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.540
This is what physical therapy looks like

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.280
at Vall d'Hebron Hospital,

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.863
where doctors say
recovery can take months.

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:39.920
While many patients here
spend weeks in the ICU,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.610
they developed blood clots in their lungs

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.030
that lead to strokes.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:45.000
So medical professionals are monitoring

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.130
all possible complications,

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.490
from the moment patients
arrive at the hospital

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.157
to the time they are discharged.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.060
62-year-old Daniel Catey, for example,

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.520
spent 21 days in the
ICU in an induced coma.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.437
He had several strokes.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:28.400
After receiving post-COVID
rehabilitation at the hospital,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.483
now he's able to walk and talk again.

00:01:40.525 --> 00:01:42.400
Many COVID patients
here also suffered from

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.567
inflammation in the brain.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:57.550
Ramon Fite, a 67-year-old COVID survivor,

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.290
is currently in rehab.

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:02.410
After spending 15 days
sedated and intubated,

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.660
he was told there would be little hope.

00:03:05.964 --> 00:03:08.600
Despite the difficulties in
dealing with the pandemic,

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.330
Dr. Sanchez says as patients get better,

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.953
medical staff get a boost.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.920
In Spain, health officials
have flattened the curve,

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.970
allowing medical experts to focus on

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.233
the rehabilitation of its survivors.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.610
Meanwhile, in the United States,

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:28.943
cases continue to climb and
ICU beds are filling up.

